I'm no expert, but it looks like write.c creates a new spellbook/scroll 
at the beginning of the writing process, and when the writing is nearly 
complete destroys the old object.  If the writing fails, instead it 
destroys the new object.  Only certain attributes of the old object carry 
over to the new one, and spestudied is not one of them, so it will 
default to zero.

